# Break and repair a result

## Section

The first mock object has an empty answer. The result schema rejects it and
gives the model one repair call. Change `backend` to `:live` to try the same
Agent with a real provider. Live mode needs `OPENAI_API_KEY`.

## Install this checkout

```elixir
jido_ai = Path.expand("../..", __DIR__)

Mix.install([
  {:jido_ai, path: jido_ai},
  {:jido, path: Path.expand("../jido", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_action, path: Path.expand("../jido_action", jido_ai), override: true},
  {:jido_signal, path: Path.expand("../jido_signal", jido_ai), override: true}
])
```

## Choose the model service

```elixir
backend = :mock

if backend == :live and is_nil(System.get_env("OPENAI_API_KEY")) do
  raise "Set OPENAI_API_KEY before you select :live"
end

script = [
  %{reply: {:object, %{answer: ""}}},
  %{reply: {:object, %{answer: "The repair worked."}}}
]

mock = if backend == :mock, do: elem(Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.start_link(script: script), 1)
context = if mock, do: %{ai: %{assistant: %{options: Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.options(mock)}}}, else: %{}
```

## Define the output contract

```elixir
defmodule Guide.RepairResult do
  use Jido.AI.Agent, name: "guide_repair_result"

  agent do
    schema Zoi.object(%{answer: Zoi.map() |> Zoi.default(%{})})

    ai :assistant do
      model "openai:gpt-4o-mini"
      instructions "Return an object with one nonempty answer."

      controls do
        timeout 10_000
        max_model_calls 2
      end

      result(Zoi.object(%{answer: Zoi.string() |> Zoi.min(1)}),
        into: :answer,
        max_repairs: 1
      )
    end
  end

  routes do
    signal_source "/guides/ai/repair_result"

    route "guides.ai.repair_result", ai: :assistant do
      define :answer, args: [:query]
    end
  end
end
```

## Ask and inspect

```elixir
{:ok, _jido} = Jido.start()
{:ok, server} = Jido.start_agent(Guide.RepairResult, id: "guide-repair-result")
{:ok, result} = Guide.RepairResult.ask_sync(server, "Give one short answer.", context: context)

%{result: result, stored: Jido.AgentServer.agent(server).state.answer}
```

The first invalid result never becomes domain state. In mock mode, two model
requests are visible. A live model can return a valid result on its first
call, so repair is not guaranteed there.

```elixir
if mock do
  %{remaining: [], unexpected: [], requests: [first, second]} =
    Jido.AI.Test.MockLLM.report(mock)

  %{first_format: first.body["text"]["format"]["type"], repair_input: second.body["input"]}
end
```

```elixir
:ok = Jido.stop_agent(server)
:ok = Jido.stop()
```

Read [Structured results and repair](../v3/07_structured_results.md).
